<div class="container masterplan">

<h1 id="top">Comserv2 — Master Plan (coordinator)</h1>

<div class="last-updated doc-muted">
    Created: 2026-08-01 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Version: 1.2 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Status: COORDINATOR
</div>

<p>This is the single entry point for "what do we build next, and in what order". It does <strong>not</strong>
replace any sub-plan — it sequences them, records what is done, and names the gates between them. Each
sub-plan remains the authoritative spec for its own work.</p>

<div class="notice">
    <strong>On navigation:</strong> every plan below is viewable in-browser. <code>.tt</code> plans render as full
    app templates (global nav + themed chrome). <code>.md</code> plans render through the markdown viewer
    (header with site/role/last-updated, "Documentation Home" breadcrumb, Suggest-Edit / Expand-All / Print,
    collapsible <code>##</code> sections, footer with Home + Go-Back). Links in both render clickable — use the
    routes in the index below.
</div>

<div class="doc-info">
    <strong>Vocabulary (read this first):</strong> this master plan follows the
    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/PlanningLanguageStandard') %]\">Planning Language Standard</a>.
    One word per level, no synonyms:
    <strong>PROJECT = PLAN</strong> (a <code>projects</code> DB row; the doc is just its view) ·
    <strong>PHASE = SUB-PROJECT</strong> (a <code>projects</code> row with <code>parent_id</code>) ·
    <strong>STEP = TODO</strong> (a <code>todos</code> row) ·
    <strong>GATE = done-when</strong> (verified before the next phase).
    The "Groups" below are only <em>dependency-ordered groupings of real projects</em> — every card is labelled by its
    <strong>project code</strong>, never by a group number. The DB (<code>/api/projects</code>, <code>/api/todos</code>)
    is the source of truth; this page and the plan docs are two views of the same rows.
</div>

