<div class="card" id="w6"><details><summary class="card-header">GROUP 6 — Infrastructure, Security & active product tracks (reconciled from DB)</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<p><strong>Coverage note:</strong> the DB <code>projects</code> table holds <strong>237</strong> project rows (primary Ency, 192.168.1.20:3307). This master plan previously indexed only a hand-picked subset (~54). The projects below are <em>active, strategic projects that were missing or buried</em> in the earlier version, surfaced by reconciling against the DB. The DB (<code>/api/projects</code>) remains the source of truth; this plan is a curated view of the important active work, not the full 237.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Infrastructure HA</strong> — <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN') %]\">/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN</a> (proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=202">#202 INFRA-HA</a>; phases A–H = #244–251). Previously buried in the infra-cluster bullet; now its own track. <em>HA for the whole app — foundational, not "polish".</em></li>
    <li><strong>Security System</strong> — proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=201">#201 SECURITY</a>. Parent of AUTH-EVO.</li>
    <li><strong>Authentication &amp; Credential Architecture</strong> — <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/AuthenticationEvolutionPlan') %]\">/Documentation/AuthenticationEvolutionPlan</a> (proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=243">#243 AUTH-EVO</a>, child of #201).</li>
    <li><strong>Theme Compliance Audit</strong> — proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=221">#221 THEME-AUDIT</a> (phases P1–P5 = #222–226). Cross-cutting; affects every template. Admin authoring guide: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/CssThemes') %]">/Documentation/CssThemes</a>. Theme Management System (proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=77">#77</a>) tracks the theme roadmap — DB-backed themes + more built-in themes from professional sources (todos #2133 / #2134).
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Floating-button theme respect (todo <a href="/todo/details?record_id=2160">#2160</a>)</strong> — the floating <em>Chat with AI</em> (<code>.chat-button</code>) and <code>#back-to-top</code> buttons use hardcoded <code>position:fixed</code> offsets/z-index/colors (not theme <code>var(--*)</code> tokens), so AI-authored edits repeatedly break their placement and they collide with the AI2 float button (<code>bottom:90px;left:24px</code>). Forward fix lives in this audit: drive offsets/z-index/colors from theme variables and guarantee no collision. Shared with <a href="/project/details?project_id=259">#259 V2MIG</a> (V2 JS/CSS migration). NOTE: distinct from the c6bd92b6 zombie-button / duplicate-arrow fix — that was a stale <code>localStorage</code> flag, not placement.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>AI Model Presentation &amp; Selection</strong> — <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan') %]\">/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan</a> (proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=252">#252 AIMPS</a>; phases P1–P5 = #253–257, P5 = v2 migration sync).</li>
    <li><strong>Point System</strong> — proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=193">#193 PointSystem</a> (phases: Ledger #194, Currency #195, PayPal #196, Spend #197, Crypto #198).</li>
    <li><strong>3D Printing System</strong> — proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=206">#206 3DPRINT</a> (phases: Inv&amp;Accounting #207, File Mgmt #208, Sales #209).</li>
    <li><strong>Buy &amp; Sell Marketplace</strong> — proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=210">#210</a> (7 phases #211–217).</li>
    <li><strong>Git Worktree System (new backend)</strong> — <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/git_worktree_new_system_plan') %]\">/Documentation/git_worktree_new_system_plan</a> (proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=238">#238 GITWT-NEW</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>Docker Image Credential Leak Remediation</strong> — proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=239">#239 IMGSEC</a> (child of #201 SECURITY).</li>
    <li><strong>Production Server Health</strong> — proj <a href="/project/details?project_id=200">#200 PROD-HEALTH</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Still intentionally excluded from the curated index:</strong> ~180 mostly legacy/duplicate/Requested rows (e.g. multiple <code>HelpDesk</code>/<code>UI/UX</code>/<code>Happygnome</code> duplicates, per-site equipment rows, <code>test</code>). These are real but not strategic; the DB is the place to see them all.</p>

</div>
</details></div>
<div class="card" id="wv2"><details><summary class="card-header">V2 MIGRATION — own top-level project (#259 V2MIG, phases #260–264)</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<p><strong>PROJECT = #259 V2MIG.</strong> Migrate the whole app to the v2 standard (theme classes only / no inline style, <code>js_load.tt</code> data-* delegation / no inline script, documentation-standard S1-S7). It touches almost every <code>.tt</code> and many other files, so it is tracked as its own top-level plan — not a sub-bullet of another project.</p>
<p><strong>Root-cause note:</strong> the current dire state of the <strong>Planning page</strong> is a direct symptom of v2 work NOT being done at the same time the page was improved. Phase <strong>V2MIG-P4 (#263)</strong> therefore fixes the Planning page <em>in lockstep</em> with its v2 migration — they ship together.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>V2 Migration Plan</strong> (human view) — <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/V2MigrationPlan') %]\">/Documentation/V2MigrationPlan</a></li>
    <li><strong>V2 Migration Plan</strong> (AI/assistant .md) — <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/V2MigrationPlan_md') %]\">/Documentation/V2MigrationPlan_md</a></li>
    <li><strong>V2MIG-P1</strong> (#260) Baseline &amp; standards gate · <strong>V2MIG-P2</strong> (#261) core/shared .tt · <strong>V2MIG-P3</strong> (#262) feature .tt waves · <strong>V2MIG-P4</strong> (#263) Planning page in lockstep · <strong>V2MIG-P5</strong> (#264) sync &amp; verify.</li>
</ul>
<p>Note: former <code>AIMPS-P5 (#257) "v2 Migration &amp; Documentation Sync"</strong> is now absorbed by V2MIG-P5; #257 left in place (not deleted) to avoid destroying history.</p>

</div>
</details></div>
