<div class="doc-info">
    <strong>Two formats, one index.</strong> <code>.tt</code> plans render in-app (themed, clickable, the
    human-facing view). <code>.md</code> plans are the AI/helpdesk-friendly reference (no template markup to
    strip, quick to read for "how do I use X" answers) and now also live under
    <code>/Documentation/plans/&lt;name&gt;</code> so they appear in the doc catalog and are reachable from
    here. <strong>Note:</strong> the <code>.md</code> copies in <code>root/Documentation/plans/</code> are
    synced from the Hermes working copies in <code>.hermes/plans/</code> — keep them updated, or (better) let
    the documentation indexer treat both as one record so there is only one source to maintain. The
    documentation-system-standard plan (Steps 15–18) is what wires <code>.md</code> + <code>.tt</code> into a
    single catalog row.
</div>

<p class="doc-muted">
    Cross-cutting hardening (W1.4, Static::Simple absolute include_path) is tracked in this master plan, not a
    separate file; it originated in <code>GitSubsystemRefactorPlan</code> A3.4 / H.6.
</p>

